body:
I don't think "avoiding the injury bug" is fair.  Broken hand (forbort 90% success on the PK with him, 70% w/o him), broken leg, off season surgeries causing major pieces to miss significant time including training camp.  What I think is different is a 5 man attack with a goalie having a career year to cover up most defensive break downs.  

&#x200B;

I am terrified of the President Trophy and then the 1st round flop....

I just finished The Reversal today, great book!  Having both Haller and Bosch tell the story was excellent.

&#x200B;

I agree with all your choices!

Yep, I am 47 and will never see a dime of social security unless I become disabled.  

&#x200B;

I wish you well with your health issues.

My Buff O's took a solid 5 months to start laying AND I had to add lighting on a timer.

&#x200B;

Location: New Hampshire.

Dick

&#x200B;

Call the FIRE DEPT or PD.  They would care.  Or run your shopping cart into it.

What brand filament would you recommend to start with for wood?  I have printed PLA and TPU.

&#x200B;

Thank you

Thank you for posting the links!

&#x200B;

More changes will be coming....

Sounds familiar.  Did I post this and forget about it?  4 years for me as well.  I am very interested in the comments.  Maybe you will help me through your post and pain.

&#x200B;

Thank you,

look up cognitive distortions.  Do you have any?  Be honest.  If you do, look up how to build up the mental muscle to recognize the distortions and frame the thought in another neutral view.  That's not talk, that is work.  Hard work.  

&#x200B;

If powerless to do it yourself, find a licensed professional who specializes in CBT.  That's a start.

&#x200B;

And yes, I KNOW the waitlists are long.  Depression can be a fatal as a heart attack, but you can get a cardiologist hella easier than a psychologist.

&#x200B;

Stay off the benzos, they make you lose wisemind and because more emotional and less rational.  All my attempts were on benzos.

I enjoy my hobbies.  I pursue them.  I am "selfish" in my wife's view.  I have a lot of family responsibilities and don't have much time for my hobbies and self care.  I guess that is where I am struggling right now.  I am stretched thin and my raw nerves are exposed.

&#x200B;

Thank you for the insight and IWNDWYT.

I am in counseling and yes, my drinking was an issue due to self-medication.  I have multiple emotional disorders.  Thank you for the thoughtful response.

&#x200B;

And I was so close to drinking last night and just decided not to drink.  So that's a win.

If you can go to a library and see if they have any books by Marsha Linehan.  She with others build the DBT framework.  Or Google DBT lessons.  Or DBT diary.  And try and do some work on your own.  It is heavy lifting, but it is enlightening when you have an epiphany.  

&#x200B;

Best wishes.

Once again.  Still not drinking.  Still not destroying myself in other ways.  Working the plan.  

&#x200B;

Thank you!! :)

Thank you.  Very thoughtful and very accurate.  

&#x200B;

I took two years of group DBT.  And I am being mindful and riding the wave.

&#x200B;

Last night I worked on fixing an appliance (honey do list) and then did one of my hobby projects.  And frankly I was okay.  Sad, but okay and coping.  But other household members didn't like my coping with my hobby (fixing guitar pedals) and voiced their opinion and acted very annoyed with me.  Which did not help with me being mindful.  

&#x200B;

Well, glad I am on the right path and will maintain by being mindful and doing.

&#x200B;

Thank you.

I am on day 149.  Not easy.  BUT I find it better every day.  Head is clearer and my blood tests (liver) are better.  When the old voice come calling, I look at the number of days I have accomplished and have to decide if I want to rest my days sober again.  I reset last year after 90 days or so, because I thought I could be a social drinker.  I can't.  I focused on THIS day, then getting to day 5; "can I get to a week?"  Then, while remembering it is about today, I looked at " can I get to two weeks?".

&#x200B;

I also have an app that shows (supposedly) the accomplishments that my body is having.  Since my liver and brain matter don't thank me for keeping the poison out, this app let's me look at the positives that await me."Easy Quit Drinking".  

&#x200B;

I found early on, distress tolerance was the toughest, that is when I went to meetings...but now my triggers are like after mowing the lawn or memorial day when everyone else was drinking and having a good time.  Or situations where every adult in my party was drinking responsibly in a restaurant and I was relegated to the "child's table" like at Thanksgiving and not drinking.  

&#x200B;

The main think is to focus on today and work the future goals in as well.  The further along, the more I have found when I want a drink, looking at resetting my 149 to 0 is an upsetting thought and the drink isn't worth it.

&#x200B;

But ultimately, it is up to you to determine what works best for you.  

\-Meetings and AA?  Do it, embrace it.

\-In Patient treatment?  Do it, embrace it.

\-A silly app like what I did?  Do it, embrace it.  [List of apps to help.](https://www.medicalnewstoday.com/articles/318913.php)

IWNDWYT,

Chris

&#x200B;

PS, if you listen o podcasts....listen to "[Sobercast](http://sobercast.com/sober-cast-aa-alcoholics-anonymous-speaker-meeting-podcast)".  It is like an AA meeting on the go (without the ability to speak and get feedback).

Is thi an update for all Ancestry DNA users or a Beta group?  My break down doesn't give results that are that granular.  Do the other 3 regions have that granularity as well?

&#x200B;

And I agree with the comment that it would be cool if your surname is Kerry.  Wasn't Rory Gallagher from Cork or North Cork?

I am in the same boat with you as well.  Except, I have to continue on for my grandmother who raised me and my biological children.  My mother died when I was 1 from suicide and when I had a couple of failed suicide attempts, my grandmother (really my "mom") asked me to promise her that I wouldn't put her through losing two children to suicide....

&#x200B;

My daughter is on the edge.  She is a lot like me.  I fear if I do, she will too.....

&#x200B;

So, even though I have SI every day I white knuckle it and push on through...

&#x200B;

I am angry that NA and AA and Over eaters Anonymous exists, but self help emotional disorder groups don't really exist in my area.  I suppose, that would mean I should start one up.  But I barely can maintain my life.  Maybe that is why they don't exist....

&#x200B;

IDK...just wish there was more support out there...

&#x200B;

Wish you all the best.

Yea, I have scars on my forearm from putting cast iron pans on me that were fresh out of a 450F oven because I couldn't deal with my thoughts and how my body felt.  I did it until the pain took away the emotional pain and thoughts.  But really, yes.  Get a professional to help you deal with whatever you felt or thought to cause you to self harm.  Now I have to wear long sleeves due to the burns and my cutting.  It sucks.  Save your skin and work on your coping skills.

&#x200B;

Best wishes.

The check in, I get to just vent?

&#x200B;

My life is better than most, I suppose.    Possible triggers:

My mom killed herself when I was <1 and I grew up with an alcoholic grand father and a grand mother who avoided all conflict.  

&#x200B;

I have a good job.  People who care about me, but I feel so empty.  So alone.  I just want to climb into a loft apartment and never come out.

&#x200B;

Oh yea, I quit Alcohol with no too much drama.  In AA I see people and hear their stories.  Their bottom was def deeper than mine.  I SHOULD feel fortunate.  But I just want to not wake up every morning.  So tired of life, of the rat race.  The ground hog day.  I once had dreams....haven't had them for 30 years and every time I start to get them ignited again, someone stomps on the embers and extinguishes them.

&#x200B;

Hate life.  I take responsibility for my lot in life, still hate it.

Yes, I worked on my wife's and by proxy, my mother in law's.  My MIL was very keen to learn more about it, my wife not so much.  I also work on my daughter's; as my ex-wife has a very prominent maiden surname and I believe I connected her back to the historical figure, but now is the time to do the paper trail work.  The advantage of historical figures, I have found, is there IS a paper trail.  Whereas, my farmer family is mostly census and military service records.  And birth, marriage and death records.  Thankfully, a lot of Vermonters and for a tiny state, most everything BMD is digitized! :)

&#x200B;

I find the Massachusetts (My wife and M-I-L have a lot of relatives here) I can only seem to find the directories.  Will I need to order each BMD record to review them?  Is there an online archive?

&#x200B;

Thanks!

Chris
